# Looking things up in SEED

Two MCP servers are declared in `.cursor/mcp.json` and travel with the repository. `seed-docs` needs
no credentials. `seed-figma` activates only when `FIGMA_PERSONAL_ACCESS_TOKEN` is set.

SEED ships several packages that version independently and rename tokens between majors. Recall is
unreliable here; look it up.

## The tools

`@seed-design/docs-mcp` exposes eight tools. Documentation is addressed as a `section` plus a
`path`, not as one tool per topic.

| Tool                                     | Use it for                                           |
| ---------------------------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------- |
| `discover_seed_docs()`                   | The section and category map. Call once when unsure. |
| `list_docs({ section, category })`       | What documents exist, with the `path` to request.    |
| `get_doc({ section, path })`             | One document in full.                                |
| `get_full_docs({ section })`             | A whole section at once. Large — prefer `get_doc`.   |
| `get_rootage({ path })`                  | Raw token and component spec JSON.                   |
| `search_icons({ query, type, limit })`   | Find an icon. Korean queries work.                   |
| `list_icons({ type, variant, service })` | Browse icons by category.                            |
| `get_icon_details({ iconName })`         | An icon's metadata and its React import statement.   |

Sections and their categories:

| Section          | Categories                                                                            |
| ---------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| `react`          | components, getting-started, stackflow, developer-tools, migration, updates, patterns |
| `docs`           | components, foundation, guidelines                                                    |
| `breeze`         | components                                                                            |
| `ai-integration` | —                                                                                     |
| `lynx`           | —                                                                                     |

## Reach for a tool when

| Question                                       | Call                                                                          |
| ---------------------------------------------- | ----------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| Does a component for this exist?               | `list_docs({ section: "react", category: "components" })`                     |
| What props does it take?                       | `get_doc({ section: "react", path: "components/action-button" })`             |
| When should this component be used at all?     | `get_doc({ section: "docs", path: "components/action-button" })`              |
| How do colour or spacing foundations work?     | `get_doc({ section: "docs", path: "foundation/color" })`                      |
| What is the exact token name?                  | `get_rootage({ path: "/color.json" })`                                        |
| What is this component's spec?                 | `get_rootage({ path: "/components/action-button.json" })`                     |
| Which icon shows a left arrow?                 | `search_icons({ query: "화살표" })`                                           |
| How do I import that icon?                     | `get_icon_details({ iconName: "icon_arrow_left_line" })`                      |
| How is theming or Tailwind meant to be set up? | `get_doc({ section: "react", path: "getting-started/styling/tailwind-css" })` |
| What changed in the last release?              | `list_docs({ section: "react", category: "updates" })`                        |

The tool surface has changed between minor versions of `@seed-design/docs-mcp` before. If a call
fails with an unknown-tool error, run `discover_seed_docs` and re-read what is actually there rather
than trusting this table.

## Offline fallbacks

If the MCP server is unavailable:

- `.seed/tokens.json` — the token catalog for the installed version, generated locally
- `.seed/llms/` — cached SEED documentation, refreshed by `pnpm seed:sync`
- `pnpm seed:docs <component>` — prints the doc, llms.txt and snippet URLs
- `https://seed-design.io/llms/react/components/<name>.txt` — fetch directly

## Keeping up with SEED

`pnpm seed:sync` regenerates `.seed/tokens.json`, `.cursor/rules/_generated-seed-tokens.mdc` and the
cached docs from the packages currently installed. `pnpm seed:compat` checks the vendored snippets in
`src/shared/seed/` against those package versions. CI runs both, so a dependency bump that leaves
them stale fails the build.

After bumping any `@seed-design/*` version:

1. `pnpm seed:sync`
2. `pnpm seed:compat` — if it complains, re-add the affected snippets with `pnpm seed:add ui:<name>`
3. `pnpm verify:lockin` — confirms the theme reset still removes Tailwind's own tokens
4. Read the changelog under `list_docs({ section: "react", category: "updates" })`
